%description:

Tcp.windowScalingFactor:too-small -- a factor that cannot represent the window stops the run with an error.

The claim: the code refuses a factor whose largest window is below advertisedWindow
(TcpConnection::configureStateVariables()); the NED does not say it (a documentation gap,
PF-3 of the catalog).

The classes: auto (-1, the default), explicit (0 to 14), invalid (below -1 or above 14),
too-small (a factor that cannot represent advertisedWindow). The code:
TcpConnection::configureStateVariables() checks the value, and the options of the SYN select
the factor.

Host under test: host1, with advertisedWindow = 131072. Observation: the error, and the exit
code of the run.

%# parameter: Tcp.windowScalingFactor
%# class: too-small
%# value: 0
%# key: *.host1.tcp.windowScalingFactor
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpWindowScalingFactorTooSmall compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.windowScalingFactor = 0    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.advertisedWindow = 131072
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
advertisedWindow=131072 exceeds representable maximum 65535 with windowScalingFactor=0
